1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,240
So, as we begin the school year

2
00:00:01,240 --> 00:00:02,500
as you know, for many parents

3
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:03,500
it's also a time where

4
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:03,840
there are a lot of

5
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:04,700
expenses for school

6
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:05,480
and we want our kids

7
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:07,060
to have the best start in life.

8
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:07,520
You have things like

9
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:09,360
schoolbooks, textbooks, uniforms

10
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,220
and other expenses

11
00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:11,800
that parents have to fork out.

12
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:12,680
And during these times

13
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:13,420
especially when you have

14
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:14,900
cost of living concerns

15
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:15,720
challenging times

16
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:16,520
we want to help parents

17
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:17,240
from low-income families

18
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:18,120
to support their kids.

19
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:19,000
MENDAKI is introducing

20
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:19,860
the Ready for School

21
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:21,260
e-voucher initiative

22
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:22,240
which we hope to help kids

23
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:22,960
from Primary One

24
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:24,540
all the way up to university.

25
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:25,460
This year, MENDAKI

26
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:27,040
is giving out $250 e-vouchers

27
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,220
that parents can use

28
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:29,340
for their children

29
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:30,500
whether it's schoolbooks

30
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:31,580
whether it is stationery

31
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:33,040
or even shoes.

32
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:34,020
I think it's important because

33
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:34,820
especially for parents

34
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:36,040
who have more than one child

35
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:36,520
as you know

36
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:36,960
sometimes you have

37
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:37,860
two or three kids.

38
00:00:37,860 --> 00:00:38,720
I think it's always challenging

39
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:40,040
to try to fork out

40
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,280
that much expense at one go.

41
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:42,380
We are pegging it at about

42
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:43,680
$1,000 per capita income

43
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:44,360
and below.

44
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:45,540
So we expect more than

45
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:47,020
22,000 students

46
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:48,560
who could benefit from this.

47
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:49,400
And this is in addition to

48
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:50,500
about 13,000 others

49
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,440
that typically benefit

50
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,320
from our TTFS

51
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:53,220
and other MENDAKI schemes

52
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:53,620
as well.

53
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:54,740
So it's an application basis

54
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:55,520
and we start to take

55
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:56,680
applications from 1st December.

56
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:57,620
So we hope that this

57
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:58,860
will do its part

58
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:00,200
to help parents and children

59
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,540
have a good start for the year

60
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:02,220
and not to worry

61
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:03,420
about some of these expenses

62
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:04,280
that would have otherwise

63
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:05,960
held them back.
